# ============================================================
# ICT Indicator repo - .gitattributes
# ============================================================
# Why this file exists
# --------------------
# tools/Verify-ModuleSplit.ps1 proves that the shell + the 32 modules reassemble
# to the exact frozen SHA256 of the compiled translation unit. That proof is made
# on RAW BYTES, so the checked-out bytes must be identical for everyone:
#
#   * without this file, a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true rewrites every
#     line ending to CRLF, the SHA256 changes, and the gate fails - not because a
#     single source byte was edited, but because the checkout rewrote them.
#
# Hence: the MQL5 sources are pinned to LF everywhere (repo and working tree).
# MetaEditor compiles LF just as well, and the LF-only BOM'd source is what the
# frozen baselines were produced from.
# ------------------------------------------------------------

*.mq5   text eol=lf
*.mqh   text eol=lf

# Scripts and fixtures the validators hash or diff byte-for-byte.
*.ps1   text eol=lf
*.csv   text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf

# Real binaries keep their bytes untouched.
*.ex5   binary
*.ex4   binary
*.png   binary
*.zip   binary
